1
00:00:05,171 --> 00:00:07,307
<i>I must do what I need to.</i>

2
00:00:08,308 --> 00:00:10,844
<i>I cannot forgive anyone who threatens</i>

3
00:00:12,812 --> 00:00:14,247
<i>Mariko's happiness.</i>

4
00:00:14,748 --> 00:00:17,751
<i>If this person deleted the data…</i>

5
00:00:17,817 --> 00:00:19,419
How creepy!

6
00:00:19,486 --> 00:00:21,988
-Are you her stalker or something?
-And I also won't forgive you

7
00:00:22,055 --> 00:00:24,557
if you try to scheme
against Mariko any further.

8
00:00:24,624 --> 00:00:26,192
Mariko!

9
00:00:27,293 --> 00:00:28,928
What? What's up?

10
00:00:29,896 --> 00:00:33,233
The person I wanted to ride
the Ferris wheel with is you.

11
00:00:34,367 --> 00:00:35,535
I…

12
00:00:36,803 --> 00:00:37,937
<i>I've always…</i>

13
00:00:38,772 --> 00:00:40,306
<i>It's fine.</i>

14
00:00:40,907 --> 00:00:42,375
<i>I know how…</i>

15
00:00:44,411 --> 00:00:45,745
<i>to protect Mariko.</i>

16
00:00:57,257 --> 00:00:58,958
-Sorry.
-No, it's fine.

17
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:10,036
Oh, wait, uh…

18
00:01:10,804 --> 00:01:11,704
Mariko.

19
00:01:13,006 --> 00:01:13,940
Wait.

20
00:01:17,844 --> 00:01:19,112
What?

21
00:01:21,147 --> 00:01:23,716
What do you mean "what"?

22
00:01:28,521 --> 00:01:29,589
‎Ah, uh…

23
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:42,769
TAISUKE SAKURA

24
00:01:42,836 --> 00:01:45,572
IT LOOKS LIKE YUKIMURA WENT
TO THE SAME MIDDLE AND HIGH SCHOOL AS YOU

25
00:01:51,845 --> 00:01:54,848
Did you go to Rinka Academy
for middle and high school?

26
00:02:02,655 --> 00:02:03,556
Yes.

27
00:02:08,428 --> 00:02:10,096
Does that mean…

28
00:02:11,865 --> 00:02:13,800
we were classmates?

29
00:02:13,867 --> 00:02:15,034
Did you know?

30
00:02:16,970 --> 00:02:17,804
Yes.

31
00:02:28,448 --> 00:02:29,516
I see…

32
00:02:56,342 --> 00:02:59,546
IT LOOKS LIKE YUKIMURA WENT
TO THE SAME MIDDLE AND HIGH SCHOOL AS YOU

33
00:03:19,399 --> 00:03:20,867
MARIKO NOSE

34
00:03:30,577 --> 00:03:32,212
SOTA YUKIMURA

35
00:03:32,278 --> 00:03:33,513
There he is…

36
00:03:51,331 --> 00:03:53,299
SOTA YUKIMURA

37
00:04:16,422 --> 00:04:17,624
<i>It's over.</i>

38
00:04:18,458 --> 00:04:20,426
My 25-year crush.

39
00:04:21,294 --> 00:04:24,063
Doesn't this mean
she has actually accepted it?

40
00:04:26,099 --> 00:04:30,069
Knowing Mariko, if she wanted to say no,
wouldn't she have said so?

41
00:04:31,971 --> 00:04:33,106
She would.

42
00:04:33,172 --> 00:04:36,342
Which means, at the very least,
you weren't rejected.

43
00:04:50,490 --> 00:04:51,658
So it's not over?

44
00:04:51,724 --> 00:04:53,660
If anything, it might finally be starting.

45
00:04:53,726 --> 00:04:54,627
What?

46
00:04:55,662 --> 00:04:56,629
Isn't that great?

47
00:04:57,230 --> 00:04:59,966
It means even after showing her
your true self, it was totally fine.

48
00:05:06,472 --> 00:05:08,441
My true self…

49
00:05:12,111 --> 00:05:15,481
What? You went to the same
middle and high school too?

50
00:05:16,349 --> 00:05:17,216
Yes.

51
00:05:18,718 --> 00:05:20,620
What are the odds?

52
00:05:22,689 --> 00:05:25,058
This finally makes sense.

53
00:05:26,326 --> 00:05:29,595
I always had this feeling with Yukimura,

54
00:05:29,662 --> 00:05:32,098
like things didn't really need
much explanation.

55
00:05:33,366 --> 00:05:35,435
Like we shared a common language.

56
00:05:35,501 --> 00:05:36,436
A common language?

57
00:05:36,502 --> 00:05:37,437
Yes.

58
00:05:37,970 --> 00:05:39,505
So that means

59
00:05:39,572 --> 00:05:45,011
the person Yukimura has been in love with
this whole time was you, right, Mariko?

60
00:05:48,648 --> 00:05:50,450
Oh, what? That's…

61
00:05:50,516 --> 00:05:53,019
No matter how you look at it, it's true.

62
00:05:54,253 --> 00:05:57,890
Doesn't that mean he's been
admiring you all this time?

63
00:06:09,902 --> 00:06:10,837
Could he be a stalker?

64
00:06:11,604 --> 00:06:14,374
Given the circumstances,
the primary suspect

65
00:06:14,440 --> 00:06:16,876
remains Sota Yukimura,
who was caught on security camera

66
00:06:16,943 --> 00:06:18,077
near the scene of Tateiwa's murder.

67
00:06:18,144 --> 00:06:18,978
On the other hand,

68
00:06:19,045 --> 00:06:21,280
Mariko Nose, who was in a power struggle
with him at the company,

69
00:06:21,347 --> 00:06:23,716
has the strongest motive to hate Tateiwa.

70
00:06:23,783 --> 00:06:26,853
Multiple employees
also witnessed them arguing

71
00:06:26,919 --> 00:06:29,122
at the office on the day of the incident.

72
00:06:29,188 --> 00:06:32,892
However, Mariko Nose has a solid alibi.

73
00:06:32,959 --> 00:06:36,162
In that case, right now, just for her,

74
00:06:36,229 --> 00:06:39,265
this guy, Sota, did this to Tateiwa?

75
00:06:39,966 --> 00:06:44,370
Committing crimes on his own motive
for the woman he loves?

76
00:06:44,437 --> 00:06:47,840
That really is the mindset of a stalker.

77
00:06:47,907 --> 00:06:49,575
SOTA YUKIMURA

78
00:07:16,302 --> 00:07:17,470
Um…

79
00:07:20,706 --> 00:07:22,141
Could we talk a little about

80
00:07:23,009 --> 00:07:25,244
what happened the other day?

81
00:07:29,682 --> 00:07:32,885
You really were in the yearbook.

82
00:07:34,153 --> 00:07:35,021
Yes.

83
00:07:36,222 --> 00:07:38,257
-I was.
-Why didn't you tell me?

84
00:07:41,694 --> 00:07:43,062
Um…

85
00:07:43,863 --> 00:07:47,266
You probably didn't remember who I was.

86
00:07:48,201 --> 00:07:52,505
It'd be awkward if someone you didn't
remember said you were together.

87
00:07:57,043 --> 00:07:58,110
That's true.

88
00:08:00,213 --> 00:08:01,914
I might have just said,
"So what?" or something.

89
00:08:09,922 --> 00:08:12,124
That MP3 player
back then was yours, wasn't it?

90
00:08:13,626 --> 00:08:15,361
Didn't you have one when we were students?

91
00:08:15,428 --> 00:08:18,264
Did it have a Kogepan sticker on the back?

92
00:08:19,899 --> 00:08:20,733
Yes.

93
00:08:22,602 --> 00:08:23,636
What do you mean?

94
00:08:32,411 --> 00:08:34,514
‎FESTIVAL

95
00:08:37,617 --> 00:08:38,818
-It's a secret.
-What?

96
00:08:40,620 --> 00:08:42,655
-What do you mean?
-Because you're not fair.

97
00:08:50,596 --> 00:08:55,368
I didn't quite understand
you before, Yukimura.

98
00:08:57,436 --> 00:08:59,071
But things finally make sense now.

99
00:09:04,777 --> 00:09:07,780
I'm glad I got to know the real you.

100
00:09:18,991 --> 00:09:21,227
Did you commute by train, Yukimura?

101
00:09:21,294 --> 00:09:22,361
Yes.

102
00:09:22,428 --> 00:09:25,598
I waited at that railroad crossing
that never opened every single day.

103
00:09:26,566 --> 00:09:28,534
Did you know? The station was renovated,

104
00:09:28,601 --> 00:09:30,202
so you don't have to cross
that railway anymore.

105
00:09:30,269 --> 00:09:31,270
What?

106
00:09:31,337 --> 00:09:33,806
They even built a ticket gate
on the opposite side.

107
00:09:36,275 --> 00:09:40,880
That must be convenient, but in its own
way, that crossing was part of our youth.

108
00:09:40,947 --> 00:09:42,748
You think so?

109
00:09:42,815 --> 00:09:45,918
I wish they had upgraded it sooner.

110
00:09:46,819 --> 00:09:50,022
Do you know how many times I almost
ran late and had to sprint because of it?

111
00:09:50,089 --> 00:09:52,858
Mariko, the reason you almost ran late
wasn't because of the railroad crossing.

112
00:09:52,925 --> 00:09:54,894
It was because you overslept.

113
00:09:55,761 --> 00:09:58,798
Even though you're usually so reliable,
you're terrible in the mornings.

114
00:09:58,864 --> 00:10:00,933
Did that fix itself
once you entered the workforce?

115
00:10:02,168 --> 00:10:06,272
How do you know that? That I used
to oversleep and almost run late?

116
00:10:07,139 --> 00:10:09,675
Well, I wouldn't say I knew for sure…

117
00:10:11,978 --> 00:10:13,245
I just figured

118
00:10:13,913 --> 00:10:17,183
most people sprinting
because they're late probably overslept.

119
00:10:19,585 --> 00:10:22,355
Well, sure, yes.

120
00:10:23,222 --> 00:10:24,056
That's true.

121
00:10:25,958 --> 00:10:26,826
You know,

122
00:10:27,660 --> 00:10:29,395
sometimes you give off this vibe,

123
00:10:29,462 --> 00:10:32,965
like you saw everything back then.

124
00:10:40,606 --> 00:10:42,575
I suddenly really want to eat that again!

125
00:10:42,642 --> 00:10:48,147
The school cafeteria's
minced meat croquette.

126
00:10:48,214 --> 00:10:50,449
-Ah, that triangle one!
-That triangle one.

127
00:10:51,183 --> 00:10:52,852
You remember!

128
00:10:53,552 --> 00:10:55,421
I've never seen it anywhere else.

129
00:10:55,488 --> 00:10:56,822
-That's true.
-For the most part.

130
00:11:15,908 --> 00:11:17,543
<i>August 13.</i>

131
00:11:18,511 --> 00:11:19,412
<i>Today,</i>

132
00:11:20,212 --> 00:11:23,149
<i>Mariko and I talked about memories</i>
<i>from middle and high school.</i>

133
00:11:25,251 --> 00:11:28,154
<i>In all these 25 years, a day like this…</i>

134
00:11:34,827 --> 00:11:38,064
<i>In all these 25 years, a day like this…</i>

135
00:11:42,902 --> 00:11:44,170
<i>A day like…</i>

136
00:11:47,440 --> 00:11:48,908
<i>A day… A day…</i>

137
00:11:48,974 --> 00:11:51,644
<i>A day like this… A day like this…</i>

138
00:11:56,816 --> 00:11:59,985
<i>A day like this, I never would</i>
<i>have believed it'd ever come.</i>

139
00:12:01,921 --> 00:12:03,189
<i>And so I</i>

140
00:12:04,256 --> 00:12:05,758
<i>bought fried potatoes.</i>

141
00:12:12,531 --> 00:12:14,800
‎MARIKO UPLOADED A NEW POST

142
00:12:18,838 --> 00:12:21,941
COULDN'T RESIST THESE ON MY WAY HOME

143
00:12:25,978 --> 00:12:29,181
‎GRADUATION BOOK

144
00:12:33,853 --> 00:12:35,387
SOTA YUKIMURA

145
00:12:51,070 --> 00:12:51,937
<i>However…</i>

146
00:12:53,305 --> 00:12:55,641
<i>I can't just get carried away.</i>

147
00:12:55,708 --> 00:12:57,510
MARIKO

148
00:13:03,082 --> 00:13:05,484
GOOD THING
YOU DIDN'T GET EXPOSED AS A STALKER

149
00:13:05,551 --> 00:13:08,888
<i>How does this person know my social media?</i>

150
00:13:11,023 --> 00:13:14,393
<i>Ever since then, I haven't been able</i>
<i>to get Sayuri out of my mind.</i>

151
00:13:17,930 --> 00:13:20,633
<i>To think my mind is consumed</i>
<i>by a woman other than Mariko…</i>

152
00:13:20,699 --> 00:13:21,734
PHOTOS

153
00:13:21,801 --> 00:13:24,270
<i>What an outrageous state of affairs.</i>

154
00:13:26,005 --> 00:13:27,873
ARTICLES

155
00:13:38,250 --> 00:13:40,519
NOSE PRESIDENT'S WIFE

156
00:13:40,586 --> 00:13:44,657
DIES IN APPARENT FALL FROM BRIDGE

157
00:13:44,723 --> 00:13:46,091
FOUND LYING ON RIVERBANK

158
00:13:46,158 --> 00:13:47,893
PRONOUNCED DEAD

159
00:13:47,960 --> 00:13:49,829
CONSIDERED A SUICIDE

160
00:13:54,066 --> 00:13:57,503
Her mother died so easily
and gave up her position.

161
00:13:58,737 --> 00:14:01,173
But in that regard,
she's not like her mother at all.

162
00:14:02,875 --> 00:14:05,144
<i>I want Mariko to smile.</i>

163
00:14:06,445 --> 00:14:07,646
<i>That's all.</i>

164
00:14:08,614 --> 00:14:12,952
So Mariko didn't recognize Yukimura,

165
00:14:13,018 --> 00:14:15,221
but he's always had
one-sided feelings for her?

166
00:14:18,691 --> 00:14:20,893
I want things to work out for Sota.

167
00:14:21,861 --> 00:14:25,664
Having your feelings returned
by the person you love is a miracle,

168
00:14:25,731 --> 00:14:29,268
but I think finding someone you love
in the first place is the real miracle.

169
00:14:32,504 --> 00:14:33,606
I envy him.

170
00:14:36,442 --> 00:14:38,711
Izumi, when you asked me

171
00:14:38,777 --> 00:14:42,681
if I wanted to date the other day, the old
me would have said yes immediately.

172
00:14:43,816 --> 00:14:44,850
We get along great.

173
00:14:47,353 --> 00:14:48,654
And talking to you is fun.

174
00:14:53,325 --> 00:14:55,794
But looking at Sota,
I realized that's not how it should be.

175
00:15:02,368 --> 00:15:04,036
Not everyone is the same.

176
00:15:07,239 --> 00:15:10,175
How much you fall for someone,

177
00:15:10,242 --> 00:15:12,711
how deep you get into it,

178
00:15:12,778 --> 00:15:15,881
isn't that different for everyone?

179
00:15:19,652 --> 00:15:21,520
I have to get going.

180
00:15:21,587 --> 00:15:23,989
The supermarket in front of the station
is giving away discounts at this time.

181
00:15:31,563 --> 00:15:33,866
Let's date.

182
00:15:39,071 --> 00:15:41,707
Okay. Let's do it.

183
00:15:42,875 --> 00:15:46,345
This is the exact amount. It was great.

184
00:15:46,412 --> 00:15:48,347
I'll text you later!

185
00:15:49,048 --> 00:15:50,416
Bye-bye!

186
00:15:51,717 --> 00:15:55,988
So casual and so abrupt!

187
00:16:10,803 --> 00:16:12,805
GORO KIKUTA OFFICE

188
00:16:12,871 --> 00:16:14,707
-Yes?
-Excuse me.

189
00:16:15,474 --> 00:16:18,043
Do you have a moment to talk?

190
00:16:18,811 --> 00:16:20,446
‎TAISUKE SAKURA

191
00:16:23,515 --> 00:16:27,586
No, I didn't receive
any request like that.

192
00:16:31,023 --> 00:16:32,758
That's strange.

193
00:16:32,825 --> 00:16:34,159
On July 20,

194
00:16:34,693 --> 00:16:37,096
an email was sent from you to Tateiwa,

195
00:16:37,162 --> 00:16:40,199
stating that what he requested

196
00:16:41,100 --> 00:16:42,534
was completed.

197
00:16:44,937 --> 00:16:47,306
REGARDING WHAT I ASKED YOU TO DO

198
00:16:50,509 --> 00:16:52,311
I'm sorry. Please give me a break.

199
00:16:52,378 --> 00:16:53,645
I have a duty of confidentiality.

200
00:16:53,712 --> 00:16:55,814
I can't show this to anyone
other than the client.

201
00:16:55,881 --> 00:17:00,085
This could be crucial evidence
regarding a murder case.

202
00:17:01,787 --> 00:17:03,789
Even if you refuse,

203
00:17:03,856 --> 00:17:09,061
obtaining a warrant from the court
will guarantee a disclosure order.

204
00:17:10,295 --> 00:17:12,564
In that case,

205
00:17:13,165 --> 00:17:15,167
does that mean
it's better for me to show you now?

206
00:17:16,468 --> 00:17:17,469
Well…

207
00:17:18,337 --> 00:17:19,838
I didn't say that.

208
00:17:22,174 --> 00:17:25,577
Um, I have nothing to do with this, okay?

209
00:17:27,279 --> 00:17:30,015
We usually only get
infidelity investigations here.

210
00:17:30,983 --> 00:17:32,584
I assumed it was something like that.

211
00:17:40,726 --> 00:17:43,062
I really am completely uninvolved!

212
00:17:43,929 --> 00:17:45,464
Have you shown this to anyone else?

213
00:17:46,632 --> 00:17:47,866
I swear to God.

214
00:17:48,500 --> 00:17:51,804
Showing it to anyone besides the client
would violate confidentiality.

215
00:17:53,605 --> 00:17:56,308
It's the truth, I swear! It is!

216
00:17:57,376 --> 00:18:01,313
By the way, does this person
look familiar to you?

217
00:18:06,618 --> 00:18:09,154
No, I have no idea.

218
00:18:09,822 --> 00:18:12,091
I mean, nobody could tell who that is.

219
00:18:12,691 --> 00:18:13,525
Really?

220
00:18:15,227 --> 00:18:16,261
That's right.

221
00:18:16,795 --> 00:18:18,764
I have to make a call.

222
00:18:18,831 --> 00:18:20,966
-Oh, go ahead.
-I'm sorry.

223
00:18:21,033 --> 00:18:22,401
Excuse me.

224
00:18:44,256 --> 00:18:46,992
Hello. This is Sakura
from the first investigation division.

225
00:18:54,133 --> 00:18:55,868
Is this arrangement all right?

226
00:18:55,934 --> 00:18:57,703
Yes, thank you very much.

227
00:18:58,470 --> 00:19:01,773
This shop has been here
for quite a long time, hasn't it?

228
00:19:01,840 --> 00:19:03,609
Yes, indeed.

229
00:19:04,243 --> 00:19:06,178
It's been 25 years now.

230
00:19:07,212 --> 00:19:08,313
I see.

231
00:19:08,380 --> 00:19:09,748
Twenty-five years…

232
00:19:14,052 --> 00:19:16,922
-Hello!
-Hello.

233
00:19:16,989 --> 00:19:19,591
-How old is he?
-Three months now.

234
00:19:19,658 --> 00:19:21,093
He's gotten big.

235
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:22,561
-I'm doing some shopping.
-Take care.

236
00:19:22,628 --> 00:19:24,563
-Yes, thank you. See you.
-Yup.

237
00:19:32,838 --> 00:19:35,274
That one has an interesting shape,
doesn't it?

238
00:19:35,807 --> 00:19:36,642
Yes.

239
00:19:37,176 --> 00:19:40,145
It doesn't need to grow straight upward.

240
00:19:40,212 --> 00:19:42,915
That shape suits it best.

241
00:19:45,784 --> 00:19:47,219
So?

242
00:19:47,286 --> 00:19:50,122
What did you want to ask me today?

243
00:19:52,057 --> 00:19:52,958
Or rather,

244
00:19:55,427 --> 00:19:57,062
what is it you really want to ask?

245
00:20:01,266 --> 00:20:04,536
Twenty-five years ago,
you were working in the Detective Division

246
00:20:04,603 --> 00:20:06,738
at the Kinuta Nishi
Police Station, weren't you?

247
00:20:07,873 --> 00:20:09,942
I'd like you to tell me about this case.

248
00:20:15,480 --> 00:20:16,615
Who are you?

249
00:20:24,523 --> 00:20:25,724
Here.

250
00:20:25,791 --> 00:20:29,061
By the time I arrived at the scene,
she was already unconscious.

251
00:20:29,595 --> 00:20:31,096
She was rushed to the hospital,

252
00:20:31,163 --> 00:20:34,466
but they said she likely died instantly
upon impact from the fall.

253
00:20:34,533 --> 00:20:36,101
-Go ahead.
-Alright!

254
00:20:40,072 --> 00:20:43,675
<i>At first, we thought</i>
<i>she just slipped and fell,</i>

255
00:20:43,742 --> 00:20:48,247
but people started questioning how someone
could fall when they weren't even drunk.

256
00:20:48,313 --> 00:20:51,450
You mean it was a spot where you couldn't
fall unless you leaned over the edge?

257
00:20:51,516 --> 00:20:52,517
Yes.

258
00:20:53,018 --> 00:20:57,356
And the railing wasn't
damaged either. In that case…

259
00:20:57,422 --> 00:20:59,224
It was either suicide or murder.

260
00:21:01,994 --> 00:21:03,128
However,

261
00:21:03,662 --> 00:21:08,200
according to forensics, the fingerprints
left on the bridge railing…

262
00:21:10,535 --> 00:21:11,770
looked like this.

263
00:21:14,139 --> 00:21:17,342
So, she must have gone over like this.

264
00:21:18,844 --> 00:21:21,079
Meaning she was pushed by someone, right?

265
00:21:21,146 --> 00:21:23,115
I can't say for certain,

266
00:21:23,181 --> 00:21:25,651
but that's what all of us investigators,

267
00:21:25,717 --> 00:21:28,253
including myself, thought
was the most reasonable conclusion.

268
00:21:28,854 --> 00:21:30,889
Then why…

269
00:21:30,956 --> 00:21:32,190
HEAD OFFICE SAYS SUICIDE
INVESTIGATION CLOSED

270
00:21:32,257 --> 00:21:34,426
"Head office says suicide.

271
00:21:35,327 --> 00:21:37,095
Investigation closed."

272
00:21:37,996 --> 00:21:40,732
‎THE SCENE

273
00:22:22,307 --> 00:22:25,243
GORO KIKUTA OFFICE

274
00:22:29,047 --> 00:22:30,315
Welcome home.

275
00:22:30,982 --> 00:22:32,150
Hello.

276
00:22:32,217 --> 00:22:36,588
Hey, is it true that Tado is taking over
as director in place of Tateiwa?

277
00:22:38,490 --> 00:22:40,826
Isn't he from Planning?

278
00:22:40,892 --> 00:22:42,260
Is that going to be okay?

279
00:22:42,327 --> 00:22:44,129
Besides, he's only been with us
for about five years.

280
00:22:44,196 --> 00:22:45,364
Enough.

281
00:22:46,431 --> 00:22:49,534
Stop interfering
in company personnel affairs.

282
00:22:52,471 --> 00:22:55,240
You seem to be coming
in and out of the company constantly,

283
00:22:55,307 --> 00:22:58,110
but I'd prefer it if you refrained
from doing that as much as possible.

284
00:23:00,379 --> 00:23:03,382
I'm doing this out of concern for you
and the company--

285
00:23:03,448 --> 00:23:05,250
I'm going to make this completely clear.

286
00:23:05,817 --> 00:23:10,021
If Keito wants to join the company
himself, I'd be happy to have him.

287
00:23:10,088 --> 00:23:11,123
However,

288
00:23:12,023 --> 00:23:14,259
the one who will succeed me is Mariko.

289
00:23:19,631 --> 00:23:21,800
You haven't forgotten, have you?

290
00:23:23,668 --> 00:23:27,839
That you and I share the same secret.

291
00:23:52,297 --> 00:23:54,533
IZUMI TAKEDA

292
00:23:55,801 --> 00:23:56,668
Hello?

293
00:23:57,402 --> 00:23:59,638
Did you find out anything regarding Asai?

294
00:23:59,704 --> 00:24:03,909
I was finally able to get through
to Asai's mother a moment ago,

295
00:24:04,643 --> 00:24:05,577
but…

296
00:24:07,412 --> 00:24:08,246
What?

297
00:24:44,182 --> 00:24:45,283
The food is here.

298
00:24:50,922 --> 00:24:52,257
Did you die?

299
00:24:56,394 --> 00:24:57,395
Eat.

300
00:25:27,926 --> 00:25:28,894
Good morning.

301
00:25:30,529 --> 00:25:31,429
Good morning.

302
00:25:40,438 --> 00:25:42,440
Were you waiting for me?

303
00:25:56,154 --> 00:25:57,956
<i>Doors are closing.</i>

304
00:26:08,466 --> 00:26:12,237
I don't think
there's any urgent work today.

305
00:26:18,843 --> 00:26:20,845
Is he waiting for me?

306
00:26:32,657 --> 00:26:33,558
Oh, are you finished?

307
00:26:35,694 --> 00:26:37,295
I just finished too.

308
00:26:37,896 --> 00:26:39,798
Would you like to walk
to the station together?

309
00:26:42,500 --> 00:26:44,970
Sure, why not?

310
00:26:52,978 --> 00:26:55,580
You're going home to watch
<i>Captain Marvel</i> right now?

311
00:26:57,782 --> 00:26:59,517
-Is there something wrong with that?
-No.

312
00:26:59,584 --> 00:27:00,585
It sounds fun.

313
00:27:01,386 --> 00:27:02,621
Mariko.

314
00:27:04,089 --> 00:27:04,956
Sayuri…

315
00:27:05,624 --> 00:27:07,058
Thanks for coming the other day.

316
00:27:07,592 --> 00:27:08,526
What's going on?

317
00:27:09,461 --> 00:27:11,630
I wanted to talk to you, Mariko.

318
00:27:12,130 --> 00:27:15,100
It's nothing major,
but I wanted to consult you about Keito.

319
00:27:15,166 --> 00:27:17,068
Do you have a moment right now?

320
00:27:17,669 --> 00:27:18,536
Yes.

321
00:27:19,971 --> 00:27:20,839
Let's go, then.

322
00:27:21,573 --> 00:27:23,141
-See you.
-Oh, yes.

323
00:27:39,024 --> 00:27:40,025
Excuse me.

324
00:27:45,864 --> 00:27:48,333
You're wearing that?

325
00:27:50,035 --> 00:27:51,169
Yes.

326
00:27:55,373 --> 00:27:56,307
I'm sorry.

327
00:27:57,442 --> 00:27:58,910
Your father told me about it.

328
00:27:59,611 --> 00:28:01,413
I thought I was doing something nice.

329
00:28:03,014 --> 00:28:03,882
No.

330
00:28:04,916 --> 00:28:08,586
I also reflected
on how childish I sounded.

331
00:28:09,654 --> 00:28:12,924
I'm actually happy
to be able to wear it like this.

332
00:28:16,761 --> 00:28:18,496
I'm sorry, Mariko.

333
00:28:20,999 --> 00:28:22,934
After your mother passed away,

334
00:28:23,001 --> 00:28:26,237
I thought I wanted to, and had to,

335
00:28:27,105 --> 00:28:29,207
become a mother to you.

336
00:28:29,974 --> 00:28:33,511
But that mindset itself
was hurting you, wasn't it?

337
00:28:36,981 --> 00:28:38,149
I'm sorry.

338
00:28:42,921 --> 00:28:44,022
Sayuri…

339
00:28:45,390 --> 00:28:46,324
Even so,

340
00:28:46,891 --> 00:28:50,195
I'm truly grateful
for how much you dote on Keito.

341
00:28:51,930 --> 00:28:53,364
Of course I do.

342
00:28:53,431 --> 00:28:54,999
Keito is my younger brother.

343
00:28:56,601 --> 00:28:59,571
When he joins the company next year,
please look after him.

344
00:29:01,673 --> 00:29:02,507
Yes.

345
00:29:11,116 --> 00:29:12,784
I'm sorry. It's a work call.

346
00:29:12,851 --> 00:29:14,819
-Go ahead, go ahead.
-Excuse me.

347
00:29:16,654 --> 00:29:19,691
Yes, hello? Yes, thank you as always.

348
00:30:26,791 --> 00:30:27,725
Mariko…

349
00:30:30,762 --> 00:30:31,596
Are you okay?

350
00:30:34,899 --> 00:30:35,934
Were you waiting?

351
00:30:38,736 --> 00:30:40,605
Sorry, I was worried.

352
00:30:43,842 --> 00:30:44,809
I'll walk you home.

353
00:30:45,376 --> 00:30:46,945
What? It's fine. I'll be okay.

354
00:30:47,011 --> 00:30:49,414
No, it's not that far anyway.

355
00:31:02,861 --> 00:31:06,865
Ah, yes. Yes.

356
00:31:08,967 --> 00:31:09,834
I thought so.

357
00:31:11,336 --> 00:31:12,437
He was there.

358
00:31:13,238 --> 00:31:15,673
Ah, no problem at all.
Thank you very much.

359
00:31:37,996 --> 00:31:39,297
Everyone,

360
00:31:39,364 --> 00:31:42,400
please pause your work
and step away from your computers.

361
00:31:43,234 --> 00:31:44,302
What is it?

362
00:31:46,304 --> 00:31:47,472
Don't touch your computers.

363
00:31:47,538 --> 00:31:49,774
Leave the power as it is.

364
00:31:50,775 --> 00:31:52,143
What is going on?

365
00:31:52,744 --> 00:31:53,845
Manager Nose.

366
00:31:54,412 --> 00:31:56,214
An allegation has been made

367
00:31:56,281 --> 00:31:59,083
that you have been taking confidential
company information out of the office.

368
00:31:59,784 --> 00:32:02,387
Due to the urgent nature of this matter,
we need to temporarily halt operations.

369
00:32:02,453 --> 00:32:05,790
May we inspect
your company PC and smartphone?

370
00:32:07,325 --> 00:32:08,726
That's absurd!

371
00:32:08,793 --> 00:32:10,295
What kind of allegation--

372
00:32:10,361 --> 00:32:12,630
Go ahead. Please inspect them.

373
00:32:13,131 --> 00:32:14,465
Thank you.

374
00:32:25,877 --> 00:32:27,578
May we inspect your bag?

375
00:32:29,414 --> 00:32:30,515
I don't mind. Go ahead.

376
00:32:31,516 --> 00:32:32,784
Thank you.

377
00:32:34,686 --> 00:32:35,720
Thank you.

378
00:32:56,307 --> 00:32:58,242
I will open this.

379
00:33:15,159 --> 00:33:16,527
What was that about?

380
00:33:16,594 --> 00:33:18,896
That interrupted all our work.

381
00:33:18,963 --> 00:33:20,865
That was beyond rude.

382
00:33:20,932 --> 00:33:22,734
You should report this to management.

383
00:33:22,800 --> 00:33:24,469
But the investigation came
from the company itself.

384
00:33:24,535 --> 00:33:26,270
Who would we even complain to?

385
00:33:28,172 --> 00:33:30,341
I'm sorry to say this,

386
00:33:30,975 --> 00:33:32,143
but…

387
00:33:32,210 --> 00:33:35,880
someone who holds a grudge against Mariko
probably did this on purpose, right?

388
00:33:42,687 --> 00:33:44,422
-Where's Yukimura?
-Huh?

389
00:33:46,791 --> 00:33:48,893
Yukimura always seems to vanish
at moments like this.

390
00:33:55,166 --> 00:33:56,367
What do you mean?

391
00:33:57,535 --> 00:34:01,139
It should definitely be
in the pencil case inside her bag.

392
00:34:01,739 --> 00:34:02,807
Try again--

393
00:34:51,222 --> 00:34:54,258
You were the one who made that report
to the audit department, weren't you?

394
00:34:56,160 --> 00:34:56,994
What are you talking about?

395
00:35:03,968 --> 00:35:05,203
Look.

396
00:35:09,640 --> 00:35:13,544
I knew something was up
the moment you came to meet Mariko.

397
00:35:14,178 --> 00:35:15,313
Excuse me.

398
00:35:17,882 --> 00:35:19,283
Yes, hello.

399
00:35:36,734 --> 00:35:37,902
I'll walk you home.

400
00:35:37,969 --> 00:35:39,337
What? It's fine. I'll be okay.

401
00:35:39,403 --> 00:35:41,873
No, it's not that far anyway.

402
00:35:45,810 --> 00:35:47,879
When is the next bus coming?

403
00:35:51,749 --> 00:35:52,850
Let's see…

404
00:35:53,551 --> 00:35:57,955
BUS SCHEDULE

405
00:36:14,105 --> 00:36:19,744
This was packed with data
that would be catastrophic if leaked,

406
00:36:19,810 --> 00:36:23,915
like company customer lists, ingredient
formulas for our main product lines.

407
00:36:26,417 --> 00:36:28,419
Was this on Tateiwa's computer?

408
00:36:33,224 --> 00:36:35,793
That man was up
to far worse things than I imagined.

409
00:36:38,162 --> 00:36:42,500
Your plan was to pin all of this on Mariko
to drive her out of the company,

410
00:36:42,567 --> 00:36:43,534
wasn't it?

411
00:36:50,808 --> 00:36:52,443
She's in the way.

412
00:36:54,045 --> 00:36:55,513
She's just like her mother.

413
00:36:56,280 --> 00:36:59,417
Her mother just happened to be
lucky enough to marry a rich man.

414
00:37:00,051 --> 00:37:02,720
Yet she looked at me
with those pitying eyes.

415
00:37:04,555 --> 00:37:06,224
That girl has the exact same eyes.

416
00:37:07,091 --> 00:37:11,896
People born privileged look down on others
without even realizing it!

417
00:37:16,267 --> 00:37:17,802
But in the end…

418
00:37:19,604 --> 00:37:22,306
it just means you can't accomplish
anything on your own, right?

419
00:37:24,609 --> 00:37:25,676
You always

420
00:37:26,377 --> 00:37:30,014
try to use someone else's power
to get what you want.

421
00:37:31,449 --> 00:37:32,750
But Mariko is different.

422
00:37:34,252 --> 00:37:37,255
You and Mariko were never
on the same playing field to begin with.

423
00:37:42,627 --> 00:37:43,527
Um…

424
00:37:44,662 --> 00:37:50,201
I told you I wouldn't forgive anyone
who schemes against Mariko, didn't I?

425
00:38:10,254 --> 00:38:12,290
-Well, see you.
-Goodnight.

426
00:38:12,857 --> 00:38:13,824
Have a good night.

427
00:38:55,433 --> 00:38:56,600
MARIKO

428
00:38:56,667 --> 00:39:01,706
CAFFEINE THAT CALMS THE HEART

429
00:39:27,365 --> 00:39:29,400
MARIKO UPLOADED A NEW POST

430
00:39:35,740 --> 00:39:37,708
‎MARIKO

431
00:39:47,051 --> 00:39:48,352
‎They're the same…

432
00:40:01,332 --> 00:40:02,166
‎FIRST TIME COMING HERE

433
00:40:32,229 --> 00:40:34,064
You're Sayuri Nose, correct?

434
00:40:36,367 --> 00:40:38,002
You were the one who took

435
00:40:38,636 --> 00:40:41,105
Tateiwa's computer data
after the incident.

436
00:40:44,475 --> 00:40:46,243
To think President Nose's wife

437
00:40:47,011 --> 00:40:48,979
was the mistress.

438
00:40:50,247 --> 00:40:52,850
It took a lot of effort
to uncover your identity.

439
00:40:54,552 --> 00:40:56,987
I was trying to see you too.

440
00:40:59,490 --> 00:41:02,092
It took me a lot of effort
to uncover your identity as well.

441
00:41:05,429 --> 00:41:06,430
It was you, wasn't it?

442
00:41:07,398 --> 00:41:08,699
The one who killed Tateiwa.

443
00:41:11,936 --> 00:41:13,204
Why do you say that?

444
00:41:15,606 --> 00:41:17,408
I was the one who told Tateiwa

445
00:41:18,943 --> 00:41:20,110
to look into you.

446
00:41:20,177 --> 00:41:21,011
GORO KIKUTA OFFICE

447
00:41:21,712 --> 00:41:24,815
A suspicious man
is getting close to Mariko,

448
00:41:25,883 --> 00:41:28,219
but he looks somewhat familiar.

449
00:41:29,420 --> 00:41:31,322
Could you look into him?

450
00:41:32,389 --> 00:41:34,692
You have a wonderful…

451
00:41:36,193 --> 00:41:37,495
spotless record yourself.

452
00:41:37,561 --> 00:41:38,963
And you're from
a family of police officers.

453
00:41:39,897 --> 00:41:41,565
But I wonder how everyone would feel

454
00:41:42,233 --> 00:41:43,501
if they found out who you really are?

455
00:41:45,169 --> 00:41:47,171
I wonder what Mariko would think too.

456
00:41:48,072 --> 00:41:49,874
What are you talking about?

457
00:41:52,376 --> 00:41:53,744
The real me

458
00:41:54,545 --> 00:41:56,113
is exactly as written there,

459
00:41:57,114 --> 00:41:58,816
spotless, just as you said.

460
00:42:00,918 --> 00:42:03,153
In that case, why did you rush to meet me?

461
00:42:04,889 --> 00:42:08,492
Because the secret from 25 years ago

462
00:42:08,559 --> 00:42:11,896
that you've been protecting
is written right here, isn't it?

463
00:42:17,935 --> 00:42:20,104
That's why you killed Tateiwa.

464
00:42:24,441 --> 00:42:26,110
I remembered.

465
00:42:26,176 --> 00:42:28,145
Twenty-five years ago,

466
00:42:28,212 --> 00:42:30,014
you used to frequent the Nose household.

467
00:42:35,319 --> 00:42:36,287
Don't worry.

468
00:42:36,921 --> 00:42:40,257
I won't tell anyone about your crime.

469
00:42:40,991 --> 00:42:41,959
In exchange,

470
00:42:43,360 --> 00:42:44,695
kill that man.

471
00:42:45,429 --> 00:42:46,864
Sota Yukimura.

472
00:42:48,465 --> 00:42:50,167
Don't you find him to be an eyesore?

473
00:42:51,268 --> 00:42:54,805
If you kill him, the suspect dies,

474
00:42:54,872 --> 00:42:57,207
which benefits you too, right?

475
00:43:23,601 --> 00:43:25,703
Hello.

476
00:43:25,769 --> 00:43:28,939
There was an issue over
at general affairs, so I had to go.

477
00:43:42,786 --> 00:43:43,787
Mariko?

478
00:43:52,796 --> 00:43:55,532
Is this you?

479
00:44:01,839 --> 00:44:03,841
You've been following
my social media for years,

480
00:44:04,541 --> 00:44:06,577
years before we even met?

481
00:44:08,012 --> 00:44:10,781
What? What does this mean?

482
00:44:14,385 --> 00:44:15,285
That's…

483
00:44:59,363 --> 00:45:02,199
<i>Me disappearing is what's best for Mariko.</i>

484
00:45:02,266 --> 00:45:03,534
NEXT TIME…
